# requirements/data-sources/local.ears
capability: Local folder sources (a person's own frames)
owner: data-sources
requirements:
  - id: LOC-001
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The system shall open a local source's files for reading only, and write everything it derives from them under SDP's data folder, which never lies inside a source."
    rationale: "The frames are the person's originals (575 GB on D:\\astrophotography); a tool that could write there could lose them (#71)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.local.test_local_index::test_nothing_is_ever_written_under_the_source"
      - "python/tests.local.test_local_index::test_a_source_and_the_data_folder_never_hold_each_other"
  - id: LOC-002
    pattern: event
    text: "When a local source is indexed, the system shall read each new or changed frame's primary header up to its END card, never its pixels, into one index row per frame."
    rationale: "21,000 frames of 25 MB each are read in minutes when only their header blocks are read; a rerun reads only what changed (#71)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.local.test_local_index::test_only_the_header_is_read_never_the_pixels"
      - "python/tests.local.test_local_index::test_the_index_has_one_row_per_frame_with_its_kind_and_exposure"
      - "python/tests.local.test_local_index::test_a_rerun_reads_only_new_or_changed_files"
      - "python/tests.local.test_local_index::test_the_commands_add_index_and_report_with_no_database"
  - id: LOC-003
    pattern: event
    text: "When SDP plate-solves a local frame, the system shall accept the solution only with at least the configured number of Gaia stars matched and a fit RMS under the configured limit, and otherwise record the frame as unsolved with the reason."
    rationale: "A doubtful sky solution would put every later measurement in the wrong place; a refusal with its reason can be fixed or retried (#71). Defaults: 12 stars, 1.5 arcsec."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.local.test_plate_solver::test_a_rotated_bayer_frame_far_from_its_object_solves_to_half_an_arcsecond"
      - "python/tests.local.test_plate_solver::test_any_rotation_and_a_mirrored_frame_solve"
      - "python/tests.local.test_plate_solver::test_a_stacked_colour_master_solves_from_its_luminance"
      - "python/tests.local.test_plate_solver::test_a_frame_with_too_few_stars_is_refused_with_its_reason"
      - "python/tests.local.test_plate_solver::test_a_wrong_scale_is_refused_not_forced"
      - "python/tests.local.test_plate_solver::test_an_rms_over_the_limit_is_refused"
  - id: LOC-004
    pattern: event
    text: "When a batch of local frames is solved, the system shall write each solution or refusal under the data folder's solutions directory at the frame's relative path, and skip on a later run every frame already solved or refused unless asked to redo it."
    rationale: "7,745 M31 frames are solved in batches over several sittings; a rerun continues where the last one stopped, reading one Gaia cone per target (#71)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.local.test_plate_solver::test_a_batch_writes_solutions_and_refusals_under_the_data_folder_only"
      - "python/tests.local.test_plate_solver::test_the_command_solves_against_gaia_through_the_acquisition_cache"
  - id: LOC-005
    pattern: event
    text: "When an investigation profile names an indexed local source as an observation archive, the system shall offer as images only that source's dated, solved light and stack frames that reach the field, each read in place and given its sky solution in the image header."
    rationale: "The person's own frames answer the same question as an archive's images (is each Gaia star where its motion puts it?); a frame with no solution or date cannot be compared with Gaia, and the source folder is never written to (#71)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3, T4]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.local.test_local_gateway::test_a_search_lists_the_dated_solved_frames_that_reach_the_target"
      - "python/tests.local.test_local_gateway::test_an_unsolved_or_calibration_frame_is_never_offered"
      - "python/tests.local.test_local_gateway::test_a_cutout_carries_the_frames_solution_onto_its_own_pixels"
      - "python/tests.local.test_local_gateway::test_a_cutout_off_the_frame_is_refused"
      - "python/tests.local.test_local_gateway::test_the_dialect_curates_a_whole_solved_frame_and_leaves_the_rest"
      - "python/tests.local.test_local_gateway::test_bootstrap_offers_each_indexed_local_source"
      - "python/tests.local.test_local_gateway::test_the_my_frames_profile_finds_the_one_gaia_star_the_frames_do_not_show"
  - id: LOC-006
    pattern: event
    text: "When a local frame has no solved frame in its folder and no OBJECT name with a known position, the system shall start its solution from the header's RA and DEC pointing, rounded to 0.1 degree."
    rationale: "Some frames carry a UUID where the target's name belongs but still say where the telescope pointed; rounding lets the frames of one target share one Gaia read (#71)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.local.test_offline_solving::test_the_headers_pointing_is_read_as_degrees_or_sexagesimal"
      - "python/tests.local.test_offline_solving::test_an_index_from_before_the_pointing_columns_is_read_again"
      - "python/tests.local.test_offline_solving::test_a_frame_with_no_usable_name_solves_from_its_headers_pointing"
  - id: LOC-007
    pattern: event
    text: "When a local frame's OBJECT name is not in the source's names file, the system shall ask SIMBAD for it at most once per run and keep the answer in the names file, never replacing a position the person gave."
    rationale: "Gaia is local (216 GB), so the names of a few dozen targets were the only reason solving needed the network; once they are in the file, solving runs offline (#71)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.local.test_offline_solving::test_each_name_is_asked_of_simbad_once_and_later_runs_need_no_network"
      - "python/tests.local.test_offline_solving::test_an_unreachable_simbad_refuses_with_how_to_give_the_centre"
      - "python/tests.local.test_offline_solving::test_a_centre_you_give_is_kept_and_simbad_never_overwrites_it"
      - "python/tests.local.test_offline_solving::test_the_names_command_keeps_centres_you_give"
  - id: LOC-008
    pattern: event
    text: "When a frame in the same folder is already solved, the system shall start from the nearest such frame's solution and use the triangle search only if that start fails the limits of LOC-003."
    rationale: "Subs a few seconds apart differ by a small turn of the field; starting from the last one skips the triangle search, and the same limits keep a wrong start from being accepted (#71)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.local.test_offline_solving::test_a_neighbours_solution_refines_to_the_frame_or_is_refused"
      - "python/tests.local.test_offline_solving::test_a_folder_chains_each_frame_from_its_solved_neighbour_and_falls_back_to_triangles"
  - id: LOC-009
    pattern: event
    text: "When local frames are solved by several workers, the system shall solve or refuse the same frames as one worker would."
    rationale: "20,773 frames are solved overnight on several cores; the number of workers changes the time taken, not the results (#71)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.local.test_offline_solving::test_several_workers_solve_the_same_frames_as_one"
  - id: LOC-010
    pattern: event
    text: "When a local frame is solved or refused after being read, the system shall record the SHA-256 of the bytes it read with the result."
    rationale: "Solving reads every pixel anyway, so the fingerprint that later shows the original is intact costs no extra pass over 575 GB (#71)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.local.test_offline_solving::test_a_solution_records_the_fingerprint_of_the_bytes_it_read"
  - id: LOC-011
    pattern: event
    text: "When a local source is verified, the system shall report each frame that is missing, new, modified or corrupted against its first recorded SHA-256 and keep that fingerprint unless asked to accept the change."
    rationale: "Size and date catch edits but not bits gone bad on a drive; a fingerprint that followed every change could never show one (#71)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.local.test_offline_solving::test_verify_finds_missing_modified_and_corrupted_frames_and_keeps_the_first_fingerprints"
      - "python/tests.local.test_offline_solving::test_the_verify_and_manifest_commands"
